          "content": [
            {
              "type": "block",
              "title": "Repository Basics",
              "order": 1,
              "data": {
                "items": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "order": 1,
                    "data": {
                      "text": "# Git Repository\n\nA Git repository is a storage space where your project lives. It can be local or remote."
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "order": 2,
                    "data": {
                      "text": "## Creating a Repository\n\n```bash\n# Initialize a new repository\ngit init\n\n# Clone an existing repository\ngit clone https://github.com/user/repo.git\n```"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "image",
                    "order": 3,
                    "data": {
                      "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1556075798-4825dfaaf498?w=600",
                      "alt": "Git workflow diagram",
                      "title": "Git Workflow"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Basic Git Commands",
          "description": "Essential commands: add, commit, status, log",
          "type": "text",
          "order": 2,
          "estimatedDuration": 20,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "title": "Essential Git Commands",
              "order": 1,
              "data": {
                "text": "## Core Git Commands\n\n**Check Status:**\n```bash\ngit status\n```\n\n**Stage Changes:**\n```bash\ngit add filename.txt\ngit add .  # Add all changes\n```\n\n**Commit Changes:**\n```bash\ngit commit -m \"Your commit message\"\n```\n\n**View History:**\n```bash\ngit log\ngit log --oneline\n```"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
